{
 "about": "Shared corpus for the secret checks: the regex patterns (key-value secrets, GitHub, AWS, JWT, and the Anthropic, OpenAI, Slack, GitLab, Google, Stripe, private-key and Bearer shapes), the Luhn credit-card detector, and the keyword-context one-time-code (OTP) detector. SuppressionCascade.containsSecretOrPII (Swift) and mci_brain::redaction::ocr_secrets::contains_secret (Rust) must both answer `secret` for every case. A case gives its `text`, or `parts` that the tests join, so no whole key-shaped string sits in the repository. All text is made up; the card numbers are the standard public test PANs and AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE is AWS's documented example.",
